{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqb3w1x0m7y","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"REVIEW LATER: onboarding KB learner could adopt opportunistic drip design","summary":"Idea to review AFTER the grader opportunistic work (2026-06-12, user-raised, not yet acted on). The onboarding learner (scripts/onboard-learn.js + onboard-loop.js + onboard-mine-*.js) currently does a BURST of focused KB-filling when entering a new workspace, but you can only do so much up front — foreign-repo onboarding was coverage-bottlenecked at ~13% kb_earned. It may benefit from the SAME opportunistic, pressure-nudge design as the judge and grader ([[note about grader opportunistic]]): instead of only an upfront burst, keep enriching the KB opportunistically as the user works (drip-learning off live session activity), so coverage grows over time rather than being capped by what one initial pass can mine. Open question for review: what is the onboarding equivalent of 'pressure' (under-covered code regions? recently-touched files with no notes? gaps surfaced by abstain-heavy gate decisions?). Related to the self-learning-harness onboarding roadmap. Do NOT build yet — user said review after the grader path lands.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T15:53:33.108Z","vec":[-0.025535164400935173,-0.03984576091170311,-0.022593140602111816,0.026096228510141373,-0.011366350576281548,-0.04750847816467285,0.09469807147979736,-0.016063040122389793,-0.05588841438293457,0.027051573619246483,-0.009201488457620144,0.0719221755862236,-0.013946951366961002,-0.01251706387847662,-0.06824599206447601,-0.011827230453491211,0.021802401170134544,-0.05499030649662018,0.02669275552034378,-0.02287139557301998,-0.08197645097970963,-0.10008898377418518,-0.03278355672955513,0.04523947834968567,-0.056387342512607574,0.012503933161497116,0.023625507950782776,0.044972699135541916,0.08862682431936264,-0.09187392145395279,0.016994021832942963,0.05883455276489258,0.022670364007353783,-0.033469442278146744,0.